---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ContactCta from "../components/ContactCta.astro";

const aboutJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ProfilePage",
  "@id": "https://maurizioturatti.com/about/#profile",
  url: "https://maurizioturatti.com/about/",
  name: "About Maurizio Turatti",
  description:
    "Twenty-five years of making technical decisions and living with the consequences. Architecture advice grounded in direct experience building and operating software.",
  mainEntity: {
    "@type": "Person",
    name: "Maurizio Turatti",
    url: "https://maurizioturatti.com/",
    jobTitle: "Architecture Advisor and Company Co-Founder",
    worksFor: {
      "@type": "Organization",
      name: "SoftInstigate",
      url: "https://restheart.org",
    },
    alumniOf: {
      "@type": "EducationalOrganization",
      name: "Università degli Studi di Milano",
    },
  },
};
---

<Base
  title="About - Maurizio Turatti"
  description="Twenty-five years of making technical decisions and living with the results. Architecture advisory grounded in direct experience building and operating software."
  ogImage="/images/og-image.png"
  jsonLd={aboutJsonLd}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="/Maurizio_Turatti_CV.md" title="Maurizio Turatti CV (Markdown)" />
    <meta name="keywords" content="Maurizio Turatti, architecture advisor, technical due diligence, CTO advisory, architectural decisions, software architecture" />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="hero hero--first">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="hero-headline">The decisions behind the systems.</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="page-content section-stack">
    <div class="section-block">
      <div class="section-body section-body--lead section-body--spacious">
        <p>
          I have spent twenty-five years making and living with technical decisions, often with incomplete information and unclear constraints. Understand the problem, find the trade-offs that actually matter, make the call that keeps risk manageable. The trade-offs that matter are the ones that show up at 2 AM when something breaks in production.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most architecture problems are decision problems that were never made explicit.
        </p>
        <p>
          Co-founder of <a href="https://softinstigate.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >SoftInstigate</a
          > and creator of <a href="https://restheart.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RESTHeart</a>, in production for 10+ years. Building software and living with the architectural decisions that shaped it.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:12px; margin-top:16px;">
          <a href="/Maurizio_Turatti_CV.md" download="Maurizio_Turatti_CV.md" class="cta-btn cta-btn--primary">Download CV (Markdown)</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Selected work</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <div class="card-grid">
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Luxury e-commerce</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              Three cities, three teams, one architecture. Distributed
              teams in Berlin, Geneva, and Shanghai needed to work against a
              single direction for a global luxury brand's platform in China.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Retail, backend modernization</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              A system that could not stop. 2,600+ stores and 9,500+ terminals
              running on the old backend while the new one took over. 141M+
              documents, 1TB+ data. Throughput target exceeded by 79%, query
              time reduced 216x.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Mobility &amp; public sector</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              6+ national traffic sources, each with its own schema and no
              single source of truth. The architecture had to make
              incompatible data look coherent. 18 microservices on AWS,
              99.9% uptime since 2017. Serving HERE, TomTom, Radio24.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Public sector</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              400K+ entities, 9M+ API calls/hour at peak. Requirements still
              forming while the architecture needed to proceed. The first step
              was finding the real constraints.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Enterprise content</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              Persistence and API layer for Crownpeak, deployed on Kubernetes
              to thousands of enterprise clients globally. One API contract,
              thousands of clients depending on it. The hard decision: an
              architecture that had to hold up over many years of sustained
              use.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="surface-card">
            <p class="card-label">Open source platform</p>
            <p class="card-text">
              RESTHeart: 10+ years in production, 2M+ downloads. Evolving
              architecture across many major versions without rewrite. Adopted
              by Unisys, Northrop Grumman, and Crownpeak.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">AI and architecture</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          AI amplifies architectural decisions. It increases the value of
          good structure and the cost of accumulated technical debt. Where
          does it create value in this specific system, and what does the
          architecture need to support it?
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Career</h2>
      <div class="section-body section-body--spacious">
        <p>
          <strong>SoftInstigate</strong>, Co-Founder &amp; Head of Delivery
          (2014 – present)<br />
          Co-founded the company. Technical direction and commercial side in
          one role: business development, client work, pre-sales, delivery.
          Automotive, retail, mobility, public sector.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AKQA</strong>, Technical Architect, Berlin (2013 – 2014)<br />
          Luxury e-commerce in China across Berlin, Geneva, and Shanghai.
          Distributed teams, one architecture.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Sourcesense</strong>, Delivery Manager (2011 – 2013)<br />
          Open-source enterprise solutions across finance, telecom, and
          public sector.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Earlier career (2003 – 2011)</strong><br />
          Alfresco, Sun Microsystems, SeeBeyond. Enterprise integration and
          distributed systems when SOA was still being figured out in
          production. Research in computational geometry and machine
          learning at the Università degli Studi di Milano.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Open source</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/restheart"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>RESTHeart</strong></a
          >: Agent-ready backend for MongoDB<br />
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/facet"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>Facet</strong></a
          >: Data-driven web framework: turn APIs into HTML, zero code<br />
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/ermes-mail"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>Ermes Mail</strong></a
          >: Async e-mail library and CLI for Java<br />
          <a href="https://github.com/mkjsix" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >All projects on GitHub →</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Writing</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          <a href="/writing/the-system-is-working"
            ><strong>The system is working. That is the problem.</strong></a
          >
          (Jun 2026)<br />
          <a
            href="https://medium.com/softinstigate-team/facet-a-different-approach-to-web-development-af884abe0b69"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            ><strong>Facet: A Different Approach to Web Development</strong></a
          >
          (Jan 2026)<br />
          <a
            href="https://medium.com/softinstigate-team/mongodb-deprecates-data-api-and-https-endpoints-how-restheart-can-help-58ea0c44660d"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            ><strong>MongoDB Deprecates Data API: How RESTHeart Can Help</strong></a
          >
          (Feb 2025)
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ContactCta subtext="info@maurizioturatti.com" />
</Base>
